;; :arch/layer says which question an entry answers. The top of the table is not
;; one winner -- it is one answer per layer, and they compose into one system.
[{:db/id -1
  :source/dataset "substrate-fit"
  :arch/coverage true
  :arch/as-of "2026-09-06"
  :arch/entries 19
  :arch/rubric "manifest/substrate-fit-rubric.edn"
  :arch/adr "adr-2609061800-kotoba-web-architecture-fit"
  :arch/caveat "The substrate properties are checkable against the cited specs. The LEVEL assigned to each architecture is judgement, and so is the rubric. No gate produced these totals."
  :arch/why-a-second-lens "The first rubric measured what the compiler admits. It scored zero axes on content addressing, IPLD, IPNI, CARv2 or biscuit, so it could not distinguish an architecture that merely compiles from one the substrate was built for. On this lens the front-end answer changes."}

 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- durable
 {:db/id -10 :source/dataset "substrate-fit"
  :arch/id "event-sourced-car-pack" :arch/layer :durable
  :arch/evidence "https://ipld.io/specs/transport/car/carv2/"
  :arch/name "Event sourcing where one event is one CAR pack"
  :arch/name-ja "イベントソーシング（1 event = 1 CAR pack）"
  :arch/cid-identity :definition-and-value :arch/structural-sharing :merkle-diff-free
  :arch/fetch-locality :one-pack-per-transition :arch/discoverability :cid-plus-indexer
  :arch/attenuation :declared-import :arch/effect-row :effect-as-value
  :arch/replay :execution-cid :arch/pure-surface :pure-with-result
  :arch/note "The substrate's own shape, written out. An event is a value so it has a CID; the reducer is a definition so it has one too; a run of the two is an Execution CID. Write locality is not a tuning decision here, it is the transaction boundary: what one event touched is what goes in the pack."}

 {:db/id -11 :source/dataset "substrate-fit"
  :arch/id "merkle-crdt-local-first" :arch/layer :convergence
  :arch/evidence "https://research.protocol.ai/publications/merkle-crdts-merkle-dags-meet-crdts/"
  :arch/name "Merkle-CRDT / local-first replication"
  :arch/name-ja "Merkle-CRDT / local-first レプリケーション"
  :arch/cid-identity :definition-and-value :arch/structural-sharing :merkle-diff-free
  :arch/fetch-locality :bounded-frontier :arch/discoverability :cid-plus-indexer
  :arch/attenuation :offline-attenuable-token :arch/effect-row :effect-as-value
  :arch/replay :pure-fold :arch/pure-surface :pure-with-result
  :arch/note "The only entry that scores full marks on attenuation, and the reason is structural rather than a choice: a replica that is offline cannot ask an issuer whether the writer was allowed, so the authority has to have travelled with the write. That is what a biscuit is. Merge is a join, which is a pure fold."}

 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- interface
 {:db/id -12 :source/dataset "substrate-fit"
  :arch/id "merkle-document-ui" :arch/layer :interface
  :arch/evidence "https://ipld.io/docs/data-model/"
  :arch/name "Merkle document UI (the diff is two CIDs, not an algorithm)"
  :arch/name-ja "Merkle ドキュメント UI（差分は 2 つの CID の比較）"
  :arch/cid-identity :definition-and-value :arch/structural-sharing :merkle-diff-free
  :arch/fetch-locality :one-pack-per-transition :arch/discoverability :cid-only
  :arch/attenuation :declared-import :arch/effect-row :typed-ability-row
  :arch/replay :pure-fold :arch/pure-surface :pure-with-result
  :arch/note "TEA's shape with TEA's representation replaced: state and view are IPLD values, so the rendered document has a CID and two renders are compared by walking down while their CIDs differ. Neither a full-tree commit nor a virtual-DOM differ -- the update set is a property of the data. This is the front-end answer the first lens could not see, because the first lens had no axis for it."}

