  :arch/note "Wins the language lens and loses this one, at the same four places: the model is a value nobody can name, the view is rebuilt and then diffed, the whole thing is bounded by one tab's memory, and no third party can fetch any of it. The SHAPE is right and survives; the representation is what the substrate replaces."}

 {:db/id -14 :source/dataset "substrate-fit"
  :arch/id "re-frame" :arch/layer :interface
  :arch/evidence "https://day8.github.io/re-frame/re-frame/"
  :arch/name "re-frame (event to fx over one store)"
  :arch/name-ja "re-frame（1 つのストアへの event → fx）"
  :arch/cid-identity :mutable-cell :arch/structural-sharing :persistent-structural
  :arch/fetch-locality :in-memory-only :arch/discoverability :session-bound
  :arch/attenuation :acl-lookup :arch/effect-row :effect-as-value
  :arch/replay :pure-fold :arch/pure-surface :needs-escaping-cell
  :arch/note "Two of its three best ideas are exactly right for this substrate -- effects returned as data, and a pure reducer from event to next state. The third, one atom that the whole program holds, is what costs it: app-db is a cell nobody can address, nobody else can fetch, and nothing can name a version of. Replace the cell with a CID and most of re-frame survives."}

 {:db/id -15 :source/dataset "substrate-fit"
  :arch/id "reagent" :arch/layer :interface
  :arch/evidence "https://reagent-project.github.io/"
  :arch/name "Reagent (ratom + deref tracking)"
  :arch/name-ja "Reagent（ratom + deref 追跡）"
  :arch/cid-identity :mutable-cell :arch/structural-sharing :diff-algorithm
  :arch/fetch-locality :in-memory-only :arch/discoverability :session-bound
